layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Bin days
heading: Bin days in Largs
subtitle: Which colour goes out this week — the same answer for the whole town.
permalink: /bins/
---
{# Bin days. The load-bearing fact: the three-week grey/blue/purple rotation
   runs in the same phase across all of Largs, so the colour needs no postcode
   and no lookup. Only the weekday varies by street, and that question goes to
   the council's own checker. Nothing here is fetched — it is computed from a
   verified anchor week in src/_data/bins.cjs. #}

<section class="wrap council-page" aria-labelledby="thisweek-h">
  <h2 id="thisweek-h" class="visually-hidden">This week</h2>

  {% if bins.current.note %}
  <p class="sample-note">{{ bins.current.note }}</p>
  {% else %}
  <div class="bin-now">
    <span class="bin-swatch" style="background:{{ bins.current.swatch }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div>
      <div class="bin-now-label">This week in Largs</div>
      <div class="bin-now-colour">{{ bins.current.name }} bin</div>
      <div class="bin-now-sub">{{ bins.current.holds }} · week beginning Monday {{ bins.current.startLong }}</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endif %}

  <p class="note">Your collection day depends on your street — somewhere between
  Monday and Friday. The colour does not: every household in Largs puts out the
  same bin in the same week.</p>

  <h3 class="bin-ahead-head">The next three weeks</h3>
  <ul class="bin-ahead">
    {% for w in bins.ahead %}
    <li>
      <span class="bin-swatch small" style="background:{{ w.swatch }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="bin-ahead-colour">{{ w.name }}</span>
      <span class="bin-ahead-when">week of {{ w.startShort }}</span>
      {% if w.note %}<span class="bin-ahead-note">{{ w.note }}</span>{% endif %}
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="wrap council-page" aria-labelledby="brown-h">
  <h2 id="brown-h">The brown bin</h2>
  <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <p class="page-intro">Brown is the exception, and it is worth reading once.
  It runs fortnightly on its own round, with its own day of the week — a street
  collected on a Monday might have its brown bin on the Wednesday, and a Friday
  street might have it on the Tuesday. Largs is split into two halves that
  alternate, so your brown week is not the same as your neighbour's on the next
  road over.</p>

  <p class="note">Check your address once on the council's checker, note which
  week you are in, and it stays the same from then on.</p>

  <a class="more" href="{{ bins.checkerUrl }}">Check your address on the council's checker →</a>
</section>

<section class="wrap council-page" aria-labelledby="which-h">
  <h2 id="which-h">Which bin takes what</h2>
  <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <ul class="bin-key">
    {% for c in bins.order %}
    <li>
      <span class="bin-swatch small" style="background:{{ c.swatch }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="bin-key-name">{{ c.name }}</span>
      <span class="bin-key-holds">{{ c.holds }}</span>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
    <li>
      <span class="bin-swatch small" style="background:{{ bins.brown.swatch }}" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span class="bin-key-name">{{ bins.brown.name }}</span>
      <span class="bin-key-holds">{{ bins.brown.holds }} · fortnightly, separate round</span>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p class="note">Bins should be out at the kerbside by 7am on your collection
  day. The council's pages have the detail on what belongs in each bin, missed
  collections, caddies and bulky uplifts.</p>

  <a class="more" href="{{ bins.councilUrl }}">Bins, litter and recycling at North Ayrshire Council →</a>
</section>

<section class="wrap council-page council-last" aria-labelledby="how-h">
  <h2 id="how-h">How this page works</h2>
  <div class="rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <p class="note">The colour rotation was checked against eight addresses across
  Largs — one on every collection weekday, from Routenburn Road to Bowen Craig —
  and all eight matched. This page then counts the weeks forward from that
  verified week. It is not a live feed from the council, so around Christmas and
  New Year, when collections move by several days, treat the council's own page
  as the answer. Last checked {{ bins.verified | dateLong }}.</p>
</section>
